'''''Oenothera tetragona''''', the '''glaucous evening primrose''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Onagraceae]], native to eastern North America, and introduced to Germany, the Czech Republic, and Myanmar.<ref name="614140-1" >{{cite POWO |id=614140-1 |title=''Oenothera tetragona'' Roth |access-date=2 August 2022 }}</ref> The [[Royal Horticultural Society]] considers it a good plant to attract pollinators.<ref>{{cite web |title=''Oenothera tetragona'' glaucous evening primrose |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/25533/oenothera-tetragona/details |date=2021 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=2 August 2022 |quote=Synonyms; ''Oenothera tetragona'' 'Sundrops', ''Oenothera fruticosa'' subsp. ''glauca'' 'Sundrops', ''Oenothera cinaeus'' ... 5 suppliers }}</ref> There is a cultivar, 'Glaber', also known as 'Clarence Elliott'.<ref>{{cite web |title=''Oenothera tetragona'' 'Glaber' |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/307026/oenothera-tetragona-glaber/details |date=2022 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=2 August 2022 |quote=Synonyms; ''Oenothera tetragona'' 'Clarence Elliott' }}</ref>

